# A method reaches the instance it runs on only through `self`: `save` reads the encoder's fields in its own code and in a
# call on one of them (`self.index.items()`), and is handed nothing else of it. Every line its body draws from the encoder
# is its running on it, so the picture says `encoder.save` on the step, closed, and on its frame, opened, and draws the
# encoder's line only from the step that built it (#461, #482).

route encoder.run
step run/Encoder()
step run/Encoder.save
step run/Encoder.save/list

line entry > run call
line run/Encoder() > Encoder·encoder@run/Encoder() value
line Encoder·encoder@run/Encoder() > run/Encoder.save value          # its own code reads `self.codes`
line Encoder·encoder@run/Encoder() > run/Encoder.save/list value     # `list(self.index.items())`
line run/Encoder.save/list > _·pairs@run/Encoder.save/list value
line _·pairs@run/Encoder.save/list > run/Encoder.save value
line run/Encoder.save > Disk(run.path) own                            # `path.write_text(..)`

home Encoder·encoder@run/Encoder() run
home _·pairs@run/Encoder.save/list run/Encoder.save

side entry left
side Disk(run.path) right
